    "latencyTargetMs": 40,
    "costBudget": 2800
  },
  "explanation": [
    "Spatial indexes (geohash, quadtree, S2 cells) turn a radius search into a lookup of a few nearby cells.",
    "Places change rarely, so the index can be rebuilt or updated asynchronously; reads vastly outnumber writes.",
    "Cache results per geohash cell: everyone in the same few blocks of a busy area gets the same answer."
  ]
